<title>UK: STRIKE THREAT LIFTED AT UK'S RRNE RAILWAYS.</title>
<headline>STRIKE THREAT LIFTED AT UK'S RRNE RAILWAYS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>An industrial dispute which could have led to strikes on Britain's Regional Railways North East has been solved, BBC Ceefax news service reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said the company, owned by a division of MTL Trust Holdings, the Liverpool based transport group, had reached agreement with the drivers' union ASLEF over a claim for a 37-hour working week.</p>
<p>ASLEF members had approved a plan for a series of 24-hour strikes and an overtime ban to press their claim. The union represents almost all RRNE's 700 drivers. -- London newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
